From 61b4abfb44e4997ee7651fe53f8b491572ef1988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Personas as real profiles; admin dropdowns follow the dark
 theme

Personas were thin records. Each now has a profile a researcher can read
as a person: pronouns; a four-sentence bio (age, work, city, home,
traits, values, what is going on and why, wellness-app history); Big Five
levels, traits and values; a weekday hour by hour; sleep (bed, wake,
hours, quality); stressors and how they cope now; phone, screen time and
the apps they live in; how they decide and where they would hear about
Aurelia; deal breakers; what success looks like; three quotes. The rules
keep it coherent (no exam stress outside students, no school run without
children, carers' stress named, household rebalanced). The role-play
prompt carries all of it. The side panel shows it as a profile: header
with initials and badges, bio, a weekday, how they are doing (sleep and
screen-time tiles, stressors, coping, circumstances), personality bars,
life and tech, winning and losing them, quotes, journey moments, prompt.
SidePanel takes a width.

Dropdowns: in dark mode a native select's option list stayed light (light
text on white). The admin shell, Modal and SidePanel now carry .adm-root,
which sets color-scheme from the admin theme and styles options; the
consumer app stays light-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
